This is to let you know that the fifth @ Play column, on the
recently-released Pokemon Mystery Dungeon: Blue and Red Rescue Team
games, is up at GameSetWatch.  The article can be read here:
http://www.gamesetwatch.com/2006/10/_play_pokemon_mysterious_dunge.php

The game is actually an installment in the Fushigi no Dungeon game
series, the closest roguelikes have come to being mainstream anywhere
in the world unless one counts Diablo (and I do not).

The game that I mentioned here a few weeks ago, that I consider quite
roguelike even though it upsets many of the assumptions of the genre,
the Genesis classic ToeJam & Earl, is the subject of the column next
time.

